Z||000000||chris6878||04-16-2000||05:38 PM||||I just put on new plugs, wires, coil, and dis cap. I am getting a code 42. It has miss sometimes and wants to "fart" at high speeds when ya let off the gas...?  what gives... <P>TIA<BR>chris||||reg||5
Z||000001||daved||04-16-2000||08:28 PM||||You probably disturbed the EST wiring while changing the Dist. cap.  Take off the cap again, and try cleaning the little plug going from the pickup coil to the EST.  Mine was covered with green "stuff" and the little plug was crumbling. I just cleaned up the wires and stuck the bare connectors back on. Try removing the plugs from the EST to the wiring harness, and plugging them back in firmly, D.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-16-2000||09:10 PM||||If it didn't do this before, you may have gotten a bad cap...... The center contact spring is defective. <P>EST???? first time I've heard it called that. EST is a signal line on the ECM. I think you mean PIM(Primary Ignition Modul), however your diag may also be correct. damage to the PIM connections or pickup coil will also cause such problems.||||reg||1
